# Auto Commit & Push

After completing any implementation task (feature, fix, refactor, etc.):

1. **Verify** — Build succeeds (`cargo build --release`) and tests pass (`cargo test`)
2. **Commit** — Stage changed files and commit with a conventional commit message
   - Format: `type: short description` (feat/fix/refactor/docs/chore)
   - Include a body listing key changes when there are multiple files
3. **Push** — `git push origin main`
4. **Pull first** — Before starting new work, run `git pull origin main` to sync

Do NOT skip commit/push. Do NOT ask the user whether to commit — just do it after verification passes.
